From: Ravi <ravi@openloopagentics.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 23:22:47 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 03/18] Add usage-limit widgets: concentric rings and stacked
 bars

Two new widget kinds driven by a file source, for showing Claude usage limits
on the touch bar: "rings" in the Apple-fitness idiom, and "bars" -- three
stacked pills, which is what actually reads at 42px of button height, where a
concentric ring gets only ~4px of stroke.

The daemon drops privileges to `nobody` and runs with PrivateTmp, so it cannot
read a user's ~/.claude.json or /run/user. Values arrive through a
world-readable TOML file named by a Path key, written externally and selected
per Account:

  { Widget = "bars", Source = "file", Path = "/var/lib/claude-limits/limits.toml",
    Account = "someone@example.com" }

TOML rather than JSON because the daemon already links toml; no new crate.
Colours are fixed per limit kind so the same limit reads the same in every
account's widget.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
